{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CeupQvjWzAid22vq5EKLU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good, baseline tests pass. Now let me complete my analysis findings:\n\n**Repository findings** — current behavior:\n- Shipment entity defined at `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-14`\n- ShipmentStatus enum with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED at `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:23-27`\n- In-memory repository at `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27`\n- REST controller with POST create, GET by-id, GET list at `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:26-56`\n- Error codes in `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37` (currently: ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED)\n\n**Conventions observed**:\n1. Error handling uses typed ApiException subclasses: `ResourceNotFoundException` (404) and `ConflictException` (409)\n2. Global exception handler at `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-29` wraps all ApiExceptions into standard `ApiError` envelope\n3. Controllers throw exceptions rather than assembling error responses\n4. POST endpoints return `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED)` for creation\n5. Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions on `$.error.code` for error cases\n6. Existing shipment create endpoint checks for conflicts with ConflictException\n\n**Affected files** — must change:\n1. `ApiError.kt` — Add error code for rejecting confirmation of cancelled shipments (e.g., `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED`)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — Add `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint with state machine logic\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Add tests covering all four cases: CREATED→CONFIRMED, idempotent CONFIRMED, CANCELLED rejection, missing shipment\n\n**Risks**:\n- Breaking existing tests if endpoint signature differs from Spring conventions\n- Inconsistent error code naming if not following existing patterns\n- Race condition in in-memory store if confirmation and other operations happen concurrently (unlikely in test environment but architecturally relevant)\n\n**Open questions** — none. Ticket is clear on the four cases and their expected responses.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change** — file by file:\n\n**1. `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt`**\nAdd a new error code to the enum:\n```kotlin\nenum class ErrorCode {\n    ORDER_NOT_FOUND,\n    ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS,\n    SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND,\n    SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS,\n    SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED,  // New\n    VALIDATION_FAILED,\n}\n```\n\n**2. `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt`**\nAdd a confirm endpoint after the list endpoint:\n```kotlin\n@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\nfun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): ResponseEntity<Shipment> {\n    val shipment = repository.findById(shipmentId)\n        ?: throw ResourceNotFoundException(\n            ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND,\n            \"No shipment with id '$shipmentId'\",\n        )\n    \n    if (shipment.status == ShipmentStatus.CANCELLED) {\n        throw ConflictException(\n            ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED,\n            \"Shipment '$shipmentId' is already cancelled\",\n        )\n    }\n    \n    // If already CONFIRMED or is CREATED, transition (or stay) in CONFIRMED\n    if (shipment.status == ShipmentStatus.CREATED) {\n        val confirmed = shipment.copy(status = ShipmentStatus.CONFIRMED)\n        repository.save(confirmed)\n        return ResponseEntity.ok(confirmed)\n    }\n    \n    // Already CONFIRMED - idempotent success\n    return ResponseEntity.ok(shipment)\n}\n```\n\n**3. `sample-service/src/test/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt`**\nAdd four new test methods:\n- Test confirming a CREATED shipment moves it to CONFIRMED\n- Test confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment returns successfully with no change\n- Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with error code\n- Test confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with error code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- **Creating a separate `ShipmentService` layer**: The existing code puts all logic in the controller. Adding a service would introduce unnecessary abstraction complexity for a simple state transition. Rejected because it's inconsistent with the existing simple architecture.\n- **Using a different error code (e.g., `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS`)**: This is generic, but `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED` is more specific and mirrors the existing `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS` naming pattern. Chose the more specific variant.\n\n**Data and error flow**:\n\n| Case | Input | Query | Logic | Write | HTTP Response | Body |\n|------|-------|-------|-------|-------|---|---|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | shipmentId | findById() | found & CREATED | save(copy(status=CONFIRMED)) | 200 OK | Shipment (updated) |\n| Idempotent CONFIRMED | shipmentId | findById() | found & CONFIRMED | none | 200 OK | Shipment (unchanged) |\n| CANCELLED rejected | shipmentId | findById() | found & CANCELLED | none | 409 Conflict | ApiError(SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED) |\n| Missing shipment | shipmentId | findById() | not found | none | 404 Not Found | ApiError(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) |\n\n**Test strategy**:\n\n1. **`confirms_a_CREATED_shipment_moving_it_to_CONFIRMED`**: Create S-1 in CREATED, POST confirm, expect 200 OK, body has status=CONFIRMED\n2. **`confirm_is_idempotent_on_already_CONFIRMED_shipment`**: Create S-2, confirm once (verify CONFIRMED), confirm again, expect 200 OK, body still CONFIRMED, no error\n3. **`rejects_confirming_a_CANCELLED_shipment_with_409`**: Directly write CANCELLED shipment to repo (no endpoint for cancel), POST confirm, expect 409 Conflict, error.code=SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED\n4. **`rejects_confirming_an_unknown_shipment_with_404`**: POST confirm on non-existent S-missing, expect 404 Not Found, error.code=SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3298,"cache_read_input_tokens":17013,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3298},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"912dfc21-6e8c-4315-b08e-e5bb9e6c5cf1","uuid":"9246ff18-44f9-4a51-b9a5-4309a68fefc2","timestamp":"2026-09-10T13:13:55.565Z","request_id":"req_011CeupQv55Q61rMTjdPyEmr"}
